---
source: crates/rustman-cli/src/tests.rs
expression: help
---
Listen to Server-Sent Events streams and print their events

Usage: rustman sse [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  listen  Open a Server-Sent Events stream (an http:// or https:// URL, or a kind: sse request) and print its events
  help    Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --color <WHEN>
          Color: auto (a terminal without NO_COLOR or TERM=dumb), always or never
          
          [default: auto]

  -v, --verbose...
          Log more on stderr: -v requests, -vv headers, -vvv everything (RUST_LOG, when set, replaces these levels)

  -h, --help
          Print help

Examples:
  rustman sse listen https://api.example.com/events --json --max-messages 3 | jq .data
  rustman sse listen {{events_url}} --header "Authorization: Bearer {{token}}"
  rustman sse listen streams/completions.rman.yaml --duration 1m
